<title>FRANCE: GTME, Eiffage to float unit.</title>
<headline>GTME, Eiffage to float unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>GTM-Entrepose, a construction unit of utilities group Lyonnaise des Eaux, and building firm Eiffage said on Wednesday they would merge their car park activities and float the business on the Paris stock market this year.</p>
<p>The new company would be majority-owned and managed by GTM-Entrepose, while Eiffage will sell most of its interest, with regulatory approval, the two companies said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new firm will have 1997 sales of 650 million francs and manage 150,000 car parking spaces in France and abroad. Cie Generale des Eaux holds over 30 percent of Eiffage.</p>
</text>
